HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmppiiii driver first appeared in OpenBSD 4.7.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The mmppiiii driver was written by James Giannoules and Mike Belopuhov.

BBUUGGSS
     The chips supported by mmppiiii do not use a SCSI-like identifier.  Instead
     they use an opaque ID and leave discovery order up to the operating sys‐
     tem.  The code to handle this is currently not implemented and therefore
     it is not a good idea to run this driver on a multi-boot machine.

